Quick wins from REVIEW-2026-11-23-d1-scaling.md, against HEAD 5f05f99 (D1 code of f0b7700).

  C21  disp_collect(): reduce the displacement over ALL K ranks, not the linked peers
       (ranks disagreed on the refresh step -> use-after-free / hang); xch_pack() no
       longer rewrites R.nSendE1 every step.
  C22  repartition(): publish J.box = P.box with the new ownership on a re-cut.
  P21  one host sync per step: no stream sync after the E1 unpack, no per-step
       cudaDeviceSynchronize (kept under SPH_D1PROF); the E1 scatter also writes
       xf / irho / p of the ghost slots, replacing k_xch_fixup and k_copy_xf.
  P22  block size per launch from n and the SM count (SPH_BLK=32|64|128|256 forces one).

Every change is byte-identical to K = 1 at HEAD: input.dat K=1 and K=8 (6001 steps, 22
refreshes); dam.dat K=1, K=4 x-slabs, K=8 default split, K=8 re-grid (3001 steps each).

Apply from the repository root:   git apply review/Claude/d1_scaling/quickwins.patch

